tests: select distinct lifecycle fixture TCP ports

Keep the loopback SSH and HTTPS probes open together while constructing
the lifecycle fixture configuration, then close both on return or error.
Sequential ephemeral selection can reuse the first closed port and produce
duplicate TCP claims before the public-stop case starts.

Remove the unused single-probe helper. Production resource admission and
UDP selection stay unchanged. Closed probes do not reserve ports against
unrelated host activity.
